ip.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3e596bfbd804277e7079268c1b6d8249aa29af6cf15ce003128a5ccfbcfe3838","event_uuid":"fb4181cb-ef6d-45f0-b706-e0e21429635a","position":{"commit_sha":"4a570145be662f62fb7708fda5cfeab4f89beeb4","position":"1785174920567501001-fb4181cb-ef6d-45f0-b706-e0e21429635a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduction at landed SHA 20e586c9e: normal review-plan returns unsigned INDETERMINATE with llm_ran=false. Both plan_review.det_invariants registry resolutions raise CriteriaError because global activate includes project.review-phase-boundaries but selected gate plan_review has no routing entry. This is a self-hosted claim-gate deadlock: the bug cannot earn the attestation required to claim the code change that repairs the resolver. No --force used.","timestamp":1785031007982987001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD RED established on current main 992b0656d: focused overlay/authoring suite produced 6 intended failures and 37 passes. Failures prove (1) explicit criterion-to-review-types activation maps are rejected as wrong shape, (2) missing/unknown review-type errors are not expressed, (3) legacy code-review-only activation still fails in a fresh process importing only plan-review, and (4) criterion authoring still writes/assumes the legacy list. No production code changed before RED.","timestamp":1785168235016875001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD GREEN on focused scope: 116 criteria/overlay/authoring/project tests pass; fresh-process plan-review import no longer raises when a legacy code-review-only criterion is active. Explicit activation map supports plan_review, code_review, or both; opted-in missing routing and unknown review types fail loudly; current project overlay migrated to explicit one-gate opt-ins. Lint passed and mypy found no issues in 379 source files.","timestamp":1785168534162369001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete and five-axis review clean. Canonical activate is now a criterion-to-review-types mapping; project criteria can opt into plan_review, code_review, or both. Legacy lists infer gates from raw overlay routing maps without registry import-order dependence. Strict unknown-type, missing-route, malformed, and dangling activation errors remain. TDD RED was 6 intended failures / 37 passes; focused GREEN was 116 passes. Full make test: 7252 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, 13 warnings in 26m33s. Final cleanup verification: 60 focused tests passed; make lint passed; mypy passed across 379 source files; git diff --check passed. Final review found no correctness, security, performance, maintainability, or test/documentation blockers.","timestamp":1785170346433837001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed as 986a644a5 (Change-Id I8f321288e68191106986e70edc5d72747abcf87c). DCO sign-off and rebar-ticket trailer are present; verify-commit-ticket resolved the bug successfully. Local committed-range review-code is disabled by repository configuration, so Gerrit LLM-Review remains the authoritative review gate.","timestamp":1785170404106354001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 983 patch set 1 hit infrastructure-only review-error because the deployed old reviewer rejects the new activate mapping before it can review the parser upgrade. Bootstrap split: amended parser/interface patch to retain the legacy project config (which the new parser still supports); 60 focused tests, lint, typecheck, diff-check, DCO, and ticket verification remain green. New commit f3dbe32b0 keeps Change-Id I8f321288e68191106986e70edc5d72747abcf87c. The explicit project config migration will follow after the parser lands.","timestamp":1785170663203617001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Bootstrap parser change merged as Gerrit 983 / f3dbe32b0 after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 (21 successful jobs), and zero unresolved comments; origin/main replicated. Applied explicit project config migration on top: plan registry includes only project.portability, code registry includes only project.review-phase-boundaries. Migration verification: 31 focused tests passed, registry probe passed, lint/typecheck/diff-check green.","timestamp":1785171707179223001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Explicit project config migration committed as bc838aed2, Change-Id I87f4cbb22eb490af8aabccba2039e718dbd0e665; ticket and DCO verified. Waited through the two-minute review-bot autodeploy cadence after parser merge; live health endpoint is OK. Pushing the one-file migration for review.","timestamp":1785171828064317001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion close-gate attempt 1 at default 16k and attempt 2 with REBAR_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=32000 both exited 1 after multi-minute runs with identical decide@then/verify finish_reason=length truncation; neither produced a verdict or attestation. Created and linked bug 9a08-614d-a9d4-4a81 with exact commands/outcomes. Implementation remains fully merged and green; continuing fail-closed recovery without force.","timestamp":1785174226831324001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion attempt 3 with REBAR_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=64000 ran ~9 minutes then also exited 1 with identical decide@then/verify finish_reason=length truncation; no verdict/attestation. Bug 9a08 now records the full 16k/32k/64k sequence. Token escalation is exhausted as a safe recovery path; no force used.","timestamp":1785174920567501001}],"created_at":1785030858658950001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"db135f1e-785d-4b6e-bdf8-ebccf142b081","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9447-b31c-e0b7-446d"}],"description":"## Context\n\nAfter landing code-review-only criterion `project.review-phase-boundaries`, fresh plan review for story 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d fails before LLM execution. `plan_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)` calls the shared overlay with `gate_key=\"plan_review\"`; the global `activate` list contains the code-review-only criterion, and overlay validation raises `CriteriaError: activated criterion ... has no plan_review routing entry`. The deterministic layer catches and skips project criteria, leaving `review-plan` unsigned INDETERMINATE.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Define cross-gate activation semantics in the shared project-criteria overlay: an activated criterion routed exclusively to another known gate is ignored by the current gate, not treated as malformed.\n- Preserve strict failure for an activated id absent from every supported gate and for malformed routing in the selected gate.\n- Add regression coverage using a repository overlay with one plan-review criterion and one code-review-only criterion, exercising both registries and the real plan-review precheck path.\n- Document the gate-scoped activation behavior in the project-criteria architecture documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With `activate` containing a valid code-review-only project criterion, `effective_criteria(repo_root, gate_key=\"plan_review\")` returns plan-review criteria without raising and does not include the code-review-only id.\n- [ ] With `activate` containing a valid plan-review-only project criterion, `effective_criteria(repo_root, gate_key=\"code_review\")` returns code-review criteria without raising and does not include the plan-review-only id.\n- [ ] An activated criterion absent from every supported gate still raises `CriteriaError`; malformed routing for the selected gate still raises.\n- [ ] A regression test proves `review-plan` can execute its deterministic project-criteria resolution on the landed mixed-gate overlay instead of becoming unsigned INDETERMINATE.\n- [ ] The gate-scoped activation rule is documented and canonical lint, typecheck, and test gates pass.\n- [ ] The change lands on `main` through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py","reason":"Parse explicit criterion-to-review-types activation and make legacy gate inference independent of registry imports"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py","reason":"Author new plan-review criteria with explicit review-type opt-in"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py","reason":"Keep the overlay schema reference aligned with the canonical activation mapping"},{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"Migrate project-owned criteria to explicit plan_review/code_review opt-ins"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_unified_criteria.py","reason":"Cover one-gate/both-gate opt-in, strict validation, and fresh-process legacy compatibility"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criterion_preview.py","reason":"Cover explicit activation authoring and merge behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_portability_docs.py","reason":"Assert the migrated project-owned activation format"},{"path":"docs/adr/0015-project-supplied-criteria.md","reason":"Document the canonical opt-in schema and legacy compatibility"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Update the user-facing project criterion example"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7cb348fe-08b2-42bc-94cd-a29051fb68ef","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["project-criteria","plan-review","code-review","regression"],"ticket_id":"3ba4-c0d1-1813-44a5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Scope project-criterion activation to its review gate","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b7a45c39-5411-445f-ab01-10d2b9674e2f","db135f1e-785d-4b6e-bdf8-ebccf142b081","926a0cac-e681-476c-b830-548a66e54760","ec6bea9e-f98e-426e-9b5b-5e947c939335","7cb348fe-08b2-42bc-94cd-a29051fb68ef","58481168-a686-4a43-8ea8-e219b7f0f42d","7974022c-a80d-4040-aa04-06fdd836ca5d","6864929a-94ef-4125-9255-aa668356897a","78591228-8ac5-46e6-bd12-11630f711250","dd2a1499-88c9-4ea3-bd8e-18190eb12dd2","8042cc94-48f2-4e1e-9eb0-61b9354aa6a6","8aa3651a-2bb7-490b-b1e9-a5c6d393e1fb","38b11f4b-55b0-4344-b093-17a755a251b4","ec1dcf9a-e2e9-41dd-95d4-4fad71311806","09ee20a9-23b7-4dd0-bc3b-1f454f35c7a3","9488db28-f652-4657-9039-7aa583f32b92","4a143dd2-ab68-49a0-8a7d-d2cd6f506d2f","fb4181cb-ef6d-45f0-b706-e0e21429635a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785174920567501002,"uuid":"f2878577-5814-4a0d-9aa0-02537dcf16f3"}